# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Copy this file to .env.local, then run: npm run fetch:media
#  Both keys are free and take about two minutes to get.
#  .env.local is git-ignored — never commit your keys.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Unsplash — PHOTOS (project covers, case-study galleries, team portraits)
# 1. Create a free account:      https://unsplash.com/join
# 2. Register a new application: https://unsplash.com/oauth/applications/new
#    (accept the API Terms; "Demo" access is enough for this template)
# 3. Copy the "Access Key" here.
# Rate limit: 50 requests/hour on Demo. The fetch script caches every API
# response in scripts/.cache/, so re-runs use no requests at all.
# Licence: https://unsplash.com/license
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# Pixabay — VIDEOS (hero showreel, project card previews) + fallback photos
# 1. Create a free account: https://pixabay.com/accounts/register/
# 2. Your API key is shown on: https://pixabay.com/api/docs/
# 3. Copy it here.
# Rate limit: 100 requests/minute.
# Pixabay does not allow hotlinking, so the script downloads every file into
# public/media/ and the site serves them locally.
# Licence: https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/
PIXABAY_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  OPTIONAL — email copy of booking enquiries (EmailJS)
#  Leave blank and the form still works: it opens a prefilled
#  WhatsApp chat and offers a mailto: fallback. No backend needed.
#
#  Set these three to ALSO receive each enquiry by email:
#    1. Sign up free: https://dashboard.emailjs.com/sign-up
#    2. Add an email service, then a template whose variables are
#       name, phone, shoot, city, date, budget, message
#    3. Copy the Service ID, Template ID and Public Key below.
#
#  These are NEXT_PUBLIC_ by necessity — EmailJS runs in the
#  browser, so the public key ships in your JS bundle and anyone
#  can read it. Restrict it by domain and set a monthly quota in
#  the EmailJS dashboard. If you need a key that never reaches the
#  browser, use a Next.js Server Action with Resend instead.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
